Conscrypt's signed APEX keeps a Panther Lake libcrypto that traps on Broadwell.
Init bind-mounts the ABI-checked CPU-portable pair over its library files before zygote.
Permit only file mount targets of the system library type, not vendor/system files generally.
Drop with the Conscrypt overlay once Google's crypto uses runtime CPU detection.

--- a/system/etc/selinux/plat_sepolicy.cil
+++ b/system/etc/selinux/plat_sepolicy.cil
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 (role object_r)
 (typeattribute cil_gen_require)
 (roleattribute cil_gen_require)
+
+; Init overlays CPU-portable crypto on Conscrypt's two signed-APEX library files.
+(allow init system_lib_file (file (mounton)))
+
 (handleunknown deny)
 (mls true)
 (policycap network_peer_controls)
